      'If no replacement exists, consider a discontinued template: clearly marked unavailable, with links to closest alternatives and preserved specs for people researching repairs or compatibility.',
      'Do not keep paying for ads to discontinued URLs. Sync merchandising, ads, and SEO when you sunset a SKU.',
      'Update internal links and collections so navigation stops promising the old product. Orphan discontinued pages still get traffic from emails and screenshots years later — make that experience intentional.',
      'Document the decision in your catalog system. Discontinuation is a content workflow, not only an inventory status flip.',
      'For this topic, build a one-page brief: audience, primary objection, non-negotiable facts, and the single metric that proves the rewrite worked. (Pattern 7.)',
      'Workshop three sample paragraphs with your team and freeze the winner as the category pattern before you batch-apply across the catalog. (Pattern 8.)',
      'Schedule a 30-day review after shipping changes so refund tags and support macros can inform the next edit pass. (Pattern 9.)',
